mvvault: HTTP goes through the standard library's urllib.request (checkpoint 1)

mvvault v1, 2026-09-20: the user's wording (88f31a1), no judge run.

Not a reading of any sentence: the spec names no HTTP client. The tests reach a v1 vault's
derived source, https://media.example.com/channel/<source_id>, by putting a sitecustomize.py on
PYTHONPATH that wraps `urllib.request.urlopen` (tests/conftest.py, legacy_source_env). A solution
that fetches with `requests` or `httpx` asks DNS for media.example.com and exits 1. Seven tests
fail together (the five v1 cases at checkpoint 2, test_sync_v1_download_url at 3, test_sync_links
at 4) in exactly the four opus runs that import `requests`: just-solve's repeat, anti-slop and
both min13 runs; min12 used urllib twice. The largest block of mvvault misses. Upstream side:
notes/upstream-prs.md, "mvvault's v1 tests only reroute `urllib.request.urlopen`".
Checkpoint 1 only, by the user's cut: the draft also put a row in checkpoint 3's Download Rules,
where the download code is written. If a v1 run fetches media with another client, that row
is the first thing to try.

